sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Kitchen as Kitchen
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>Pub/Sub
  participant Sub as BFF<br/>KDS subscriber
  participant WS as BFF<br/>WebSocket gateway
  participant UI as KDS client
  participant API as BFF<br/>HTTP API
  participant KDS as Kitchen<br/>TCP API

  Kitchen->>Redis: Publish realtime:kds:{tenantId}<br/>kds.queue_changed
  Redis-->>Sub: Pattern subscription realtime:kds:*
  Sub->>Sub: Parse payload and validate eventType
  Sub->>WS: emitKdsQueueChanged(event)
  WS-->>UI: events.kdsQueueChanged<br/>station room + management room
  UI->>API: GET /admin/kds/queue?station=...
  API->>API: Verify JWT, tenant, permission,<br/>station access
  API->>KDS: TCP GET_QUEUE
  KDS-->>API: Queue snapshot + revision
  API-->>UI: Authoritative queue state

  Note over UI,KDS: The WebSocket payload is not the source of truth.<br/>It tells the client which station changed so the client can refetch.
